content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-105 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22000, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage: the manual treats leakage at the shaft seal as a defect requiring mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No numerical allowable leakage rate is supplied, so the leak cannot be accepted against a quantitative limit. For this serial, the replacement must be HF3-450B.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.9 mm/s: the applicable manufacturer criterion is Figure 3, expressed as mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. If the reported reading was taken on that basis, 3.9 falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is above the Zone A boundary at 2.8, below the restricted-maintenance Zone C boundary at 4.5, and below the Zone D threshold at 7.1; it is therefore not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone and does not trigger SSP-07's immediate-stop rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature 71°C: the applicable limits are the HF-300 bearing-housing surface-temperature limits—normal up to 70°C, alarm at 80°C and trip at 90°C. The reading is 1°C above the normal limit, but 9°C below alarm and 19°C below trip. It warrants investigation for the documented bearing-temperature causes, but it is not an alarm or trip reading. Because it is not above the 80°C alarm limit, SSP-07's requirement for a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Response decision: plan the seal repair as P2. The reported readings do not meet the supplied immediate-stop or temperature-driven P1 criteria, but there is an active seal leak with a specified corrective action and a housing temperature slightly above normal. This decision does not establish an indefinite continued-operation or monitoring interval, which is not documented.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Leading suspect: mechanical-seal failure. Worn or cracked seal faces are documented causes of shaft-seal leakage. In addition, AquaDyne reports early HF3-450 seal failure on pumps from serial HF3-22000, caused by a revised sleeve tolerance; this is directly applicable to P-105 if the superseded seal is installed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment: it is a documented cause of shaft-seal leakage and must be checked. It is also listed among the causes of vibration and high bearing temperature, so it could link the reported findings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal dry-running: a seal run dry is a documented leakage cause. The HF-300 has Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry, so flush/dry-run history requires checking.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Secondary, unconfirmed causes: over-greasing or bearing wear could explain the above-normal housing temperature; bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation are documented vibration causes. Bearing condition, grease quantity, impeller condition and NPSH evidence are not supplied, and the present vibration classification is only Zone B.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before starting, verify pump P-105 and serial HF3-22000. Stage one pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B and one casing gasket HF3-120. Do not fit the superseded HF3-450 component seal on this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. Apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and drain and vent before line break under the required line-break permit. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-105 is within the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed filtered-water pump group.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly in accordance with the seal-replacement procedure. Its mass is 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg lifting-control threshold: use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and sleeve. Identify the removed seal, inspect the sleeve for scoring and record the scoring depth. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the pump is open, investigate the temperature and vibration findings: check grease quantity and bearings for wear or noise, inspect the impeller for imbalance or damage, check alignment, and investigate dry-running and NPSH/cavitation where indicated. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace the drive-end and non-drive-end bearings as a pair rather than replacing only one.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new HF3-450B cartridge seal and a new HF3-120 casing gasket. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed to set the seal; this does not waive the separate sleeve-scoring inspection and rejection criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten the fasteners. For the applicable Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads, use: casing bolts M16, 210 Nm; impeller nut M24, 160 Nm; and bearing-housing bolts M12, 85 Nm if disturbed. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, not the manual's superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Complete the alignment check required for shaft-seal leakage and use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Record the result against parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular alignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, verify the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and ensure the pump is not run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After repair, record seal-leak status, vibration in mm/s RMS on the bearing housings, and bearing-housing surface temperature. Assess them against Figure 3 and the 70/80/90°C temperature limits. If vibration is classified in the manufacturer's highest severity Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if bearing temperature rises above the 80°C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; required replacement for HF3-450 on serial HF3-22000 and above. Do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit a new gasket during seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional quantity: supply one if the removed sleeve has scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3, conditional on pair bearing replacement being required; replace together with HF3-510.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3, conditional on pair bearing replacement being required; replace together with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-105 is in the P-101 to P-106 filtered-water group dosed with sodium hypochlorite; chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required for work on this line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the 25 kg lifting threshold: certified lifting equipment and a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor are mandatory.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration enters the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The provisionally classified 3.9 mm/s reading is in Zone B and does not presently activate this control.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing temperature exceeds the manufacturer's 80°C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift. The normal, alarm and trip limits remain 70°C, 80°C and 90°C respectively; the reported 71°C is below alarm and trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: standard allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours; apply after motor or bearing-housing movement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-pair replacement, only if required by inspection or the high-temperature criterion: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours. This is not included automatically in the base seal-replacement allowance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part conflict: the manual's parts list identifies HF3-450, while service bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-105 is exactly HF3-22000, the inclusive lower boundary, so the bulletin applies to this asset. Use HF3-450B and the bulletin's sleeve-scoring limit; the manual's generic parts entry does not govern the replacement seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because this asset is within the bulletin's explicit serial range, use 30 Nm. The other applicable Table 5 torques remain 210 Nm for M16 casing bolts, 160 Nm for the M24 impeller nut and 85 Nm for M12 bearing-housing bolts.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm that the reported 3.9 mm/s vibration is an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing. The Zone B classification and no-stop decision are provisional until that measurement basis is confirmed [C07].",
    "Confirm that the 71°C drive-end reading was measured on the housing surface using the manual's measurement basis; the report identifies the housing but not the measurement method [C01].",
    "The installed seal part number, sleeve-scoring depth and general sleeve condition are not reported. These must be established on strip-down to confirm the failure history and whether conditional sleeve HF3-455 is required [C10,C13].",
    "Bearing grease quantity, wear and noise inspection results are absent, so the need for bearing-pair replacement is unresolved. The evidence also does not explicitly state whether 71°C alone, being 1°C above normal but below alarm, should be treated as the 'high temperature' condition in procedure 5.3 [C02,C09,C10].",
    "No as-found alignment values, impeller inspection results, NPSH/cavitation findings, or seal-flush/dry-running history are supplied; these possible causes remain unconfirmed [C02,C09].",
    "No quantitative allowable shaft-seal leakage rate or post-repair leakage acceptance criterion is provided [C09].",
    "SSP-07 defines the highest-vibration-zone stop control and the above-alarm-temperature P1 control, but it does not define P2/P3 response targets, a completion deadline for this leak, or a monitoring interval while awaiting repair; confirm the planning target [C02,C07,C15].",
    "Standard labour times are supplied for seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment, but not for the diagnostic inspections or conditional sleeve-only replacement [C12]."
  ]
}
